  "name": null,
  "problem": "A laboratory test for a particular disease is conducted on some patients. Of the tested patients, $97%$ of those infected and $1%$ of those not infected tested positive for the disease. Only $1%$ of the entire population is infected with the disease. What is the probability that a randomly chosen patient that tested positive is infected? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
